  "worked_solution": "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $det(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-12-9 \\\\  & =-21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}=-\\frac{1}{21}.\n$$",
